From a2b9b49d34e99adf3c2b1d2171bd9ca10c2808f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:37:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 908/913] drivers: stm32_remoteproc: fix rproc resource leak in
 probe

When a probed remote processor has ns_loading set and either lacks a
"#reset-cells" DT property or a cdata->pm callback, the allocated
rproc instance was never inserted into rproc_list, registered with the
PM framework, nor kept alive by the reset-controller provider,
leaving it unreachable and leaked on the success return path.

Add the memory free for rproc->dma_ranges and register the rproc
whatever the ns_loading value.

Coverity issue: CID 1200357: Resource leak

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a248e67075945f13386deceb5887f88a3b32b06c drivers: stm32_remoteproc: fix rproc resource leak in probe]
Signed-off-by: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ib2fa589b51db3fd673d24e181bdc061e8c23eac9
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/619057
Tested-by: Sebastien PASDELOUP <sebastien.pasdeloup-ext@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_remoteproc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_remoteproc.c b/core/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_remoteproc.c
index 78fc5fee0..f332c2ba4 100644
--- a/core/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_remoteproc.c
+++ b/core/drivers/remoteproc/stm32_remoteproc.c
@@ -709,6 +709,7 @@ TEE_Result stm32_rproc_release_mem(uint32_t rproc_id)
 static void stm32_rproc_cleanup(struct stm32_rproc_instance *rproc)
 {
 	stm32_rproc_free_regions(rproc);
+	free(rproc->dma_ranges);
 	free(rproc);
 }
 
@@ -915,8 +916,7 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_rproc_probe(const void *fdt, int node,
 
 	stm32_rproc_a35ss_cfg(rproc);
 
-	if (!rproc->cdata->ns_loading)
-		SLIST_INSERT_HEAD(&rproc_list, rproc, link);
+	SLIST_INSERT_HEAD(&rproc_list, rproc, link);
 
 	if (rproc->cdata->pm)
 		register_pm_driver_cb(rproc->cdata->pm, rproc, "stm32-rproc");
-- 
